  "reason": "Evidence: Only two experiments are complete. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% acc, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. config_010 (image_only, resnet50) achieves only 20.8% acc, showing image is very weak. Critical uncertainty: we have no data on whether multiprofile (vs singleprofile) provides meaningful signal, and this axis affects every downstream configuration. Question tested: Does aggregating multiple cell profiles (via avgpool) with the same PCA-2000 RNA encoder improve over the single-profile baseline? config_002 is directly comparable to config_001, isolating the profile-setting + aggregation variable. Why best next experiment: With only 2 data points, the highest-value information is resolving whether the multiprofile branch of the search space is worth pursuing at all. A positive result opens a large, promising sub-space (configs 002-009, 018-051); a null result lets us prune it and focus budget on encoder and fusion choices. It is a low-variance, clean A/B comparison that maximally reduces uncertainty per experiment."
}

